#fixedname "Syluné Silverhand"
#descr "Syluné, also known as the Witch of Shadowdale, was the eldest of the Seven Sisters - the immortal daughters of Mystra, goddess of magic. Among her most famous younger siblings were Alustriel, Laeral, and Alassra, also known as The Simbul. 

Syluné decided that she could best serve Mystra by settling down and nurturing a community to show that magic was more than just a weapon. She hoped to one day set up a magical school, as well. Mystra agreed, and so Syluné wandered the Realms for centuries, enhancing her own magecraft and looking for a suitable place to achieve her goal. In her quest, she trained under hermits, druids, priests, and liches, as well as other mages. She spent a lot of time in the east in Thay (in disguise), with the witches of Rashemen, and she visited the land of Kara-Tur several times as well. She made many powerful friends during these years, and was involved in the conflict between demigods after coming into the possession of the Scepter of Savras and was given the the gift to transform herself into a Silver Dragon by Azuth when she relinquished the artifact into his care. 

She eventually chose Shadowdale as her home. There, she married Aumry Obarskyr, the leader of the Dale at the time. Together, they ruled peacefully for nearly 40 years, with Syluné's influence among the elves in Evereska helping to save Shadowdale many times from would-be conquerors. Aumry's assassination by agents of the Zhentarim in 1339 DR would bring an end to their benevolent rule, but while other rulers would arise in name, none would ever truly replace the Witch of Shadowdale." 
