-- 7442 -- Storm Silverhand
#newmonster 7442
#copystats 3833 -- Divine Sibyl
#spr1 "ForgottenRealms/stormsilverhand.tga"
#spr2 "ForgottenRealms/stormsilverhand2.tga"
#clearspec
#name "The Bard of Shadowdale"
#fixedname "Storm Silverhand"
#descr "Storm Silverhand, known as The Bard of Shadowdale, was one of the Seven Sisters and a daughter and Chosen of Mystra. She was known and loved by many in her home of Shadowdale and elsewhere in Faerûn. High-spirited, fearless, and merry, Storm possessed a lust for life that grew when she saw others' happy. She also had a vengeful streak, which she aimed at the Zhentarim and any others who stole, lied, carelessly started fires or otherwise despoiled the land. 

Storm was born, along with her sisters, in 764 DR by miraculous conception gifted by Mystra, goddess of magic. She joined Dove and Laeral in the foster care of Elminster, the great Sage of Shadowdale, following the death of her biological mother. She proved to be a wild child, and Elminster struggled to keep her in line while he was also traveling the planes and righting wrongs. Storm ran away from him several times until she was kidnapped by a mage who altered her appearance and took her as a slave. So, rather than benefit from the tutelage of Elminster, who failed to locate the girl, Storm lived as a slave in the south of Faerûn. There, she danced in bazaars and festhalls until she managed to steal a flying carpet and returned to Elminster, brazenly demanding he restore her true features and take her back under his care.

Bored, Storm eventually joined her sister Dove as a very involved member of the Harpers and was instrumental in the reformation of the group in 1022 DR. Among her many legendary accomplishments was her climactic defeat of Iyachtu Xvim, fiendish progeny of the dark god, Bane. She aided her sister Alustriel's rise to power in the Silver Marches. After centuries of adventuring, she chose to settle down in Shadowdale alongside her sister, Syluné, and it was their choice of Shadowdale that prompted Elminster to make the region his home on the material plane." 
