#descr "Drow began construction of the Twisted Tower in −2600 DR, and completed it in −2549 DR. It was expanded at least twice under their sovereigny. In −331 DR, elven armies broke through the Twisted Tower's defenses and occupied the stronghold, but the drow captured the legendary elven artifact, The Soldier's Blade, in the process. The tower was handed over to a contingent of good-aligned dark elves who rededicated it as a temple to Eilistraee. 

The drow took advantage of the fall of Myth Drannor during the Weeping War in 713 DR and openly seized the Tower once more, refounding the Lands Under Shadow. Their reestablished surface realm only lasted two centuries when, in the Year of the Plough, 906 DR, the Tower's drow occupants were besieged and after a full year of struggle, had their well poisoned by a human slave. Forced to flee back to the Underdark, the drow abaondoned the Twisted Tower to the humans conquerers. The great water wizard konwn simply as Ashaba became the first lord of the newly founded Shadowdale and chose the Twisted Tower as his keep and court. In 940 DR, the Twisted Tower was renamed to the Twisted Tower of Ashaba in his honor after Ashaba merged with a nearby river and became a spirit and protector of the land. 

Throughout the four centuries of human occupation since, the Twisted Tower has retained its place as the royal court and has long relied on the powerful mages apprenticed under Storm and Syluné Silverhand and Elminster, the Sage of Shadowdale. Alongside their vital role in the study of magic, Mages of the Twisted Tower are also well-versed in the enchantment of magical arms and armor."
